    <string name="installer_help"><b>What is BAI?</b>\nBAI (Bundle APKs Installer) is an app that lets you install multiple APKs as if it was a single package. This is useful for installing apps that are distributed as App Bundles since Android provides no built-in way to install them from sources other than Google Play.\n\n<b>How to use BAI?</b>\nClick \"Install APKs\" button and select base APK and additional configuration-specific APKs or a ZIP archive that contains all required APKs, then click \"Select\" button to start installation process.\n\n<b>.apks</b>\nYou can rename a .zip archive that contains .apk files to .apks (e.g.: somesplitapp.zip -&gt; somesplitapp.apks), so it can be opened with BAI from other apps.\n\n<b>Installing apps from external storage</b>\nYou can long click install button to select files via system file picker that supports external storage.</string>
