    <string name="backup_warning"><b>Managed backups are currently in beta, please report issues in BAI\'s GitHub repo (you can find the link on about screen)</b>\n\n<b>Backup files format</b>\nBAI backups apps as .apks files (which are just ZIP archives with .apk files) with some meta information added to the archive (such as app name and icon). Backed up .apks files can still be installed as normal .apks files (because they are normal .apks files, except for some additional files in the archive which are ignored by installer)\n\n<b>What is backed up</b>\nCurrently BAI backups only apps APK files (no data/obb/etc)\n\n<b>External changes to backup directory</b>\nBAI doesn\'t automatically keep track of external changes done to files in the backup directory. So, if you\'ve changed them outside of BAI, use reindex option in 3-dots menu at the top right of backup screen to rescan backups directory.\n\n<b>You can always open this help from the 3-dots menu at the top right of backup screen</b></string>
